                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "10372864",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198003106630",
                            "num_reviews": 67,
                            "playtime_forever": 206,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 195,
                            "last_played": 1402089848
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game/simulator packs the same punch as most unfinished products released on Steam.\nAlthough I've had my share of fun with it, there are just too many faulty elements to make it sustainable.\nI recommend this game if the price is of trivial importance and you have an hour to kill.\n\nPros:\n-The info on the Store Page seems correct.\n-Graphics looks alright\n-Scenery is nice\n-The music is smooth (country'ish)\n-The driving itself is comforting\n-You get to drive a truck\n\nCons:\n-This product probably skipped beta.\n-The game spits and stutters. With all settings turned way down, my gaming rig still coughs.\n-Physics needs work. Although driving is fun enough, there are a lot of exciting places to get stuck and crash into.\n-Camera view is an endless pain in the boot. There are no modes like chase-cam etc.\n-When you finish a mission by offloading the goods, your vehicle will most likely stop working. $500 tow fee, just to rub it in.\nThis also kept reverting my selection of the bigger truck to the one that you start with.\n-AI vehicles are unpredictable and will not hesitate to slow down if you tailgate them, just to make absolutely sure that you'll either ram them or perform some spastic manouvers.\n-The game does indeed crash at random without spitting any error messages. Game progress reverts to last clean exit.",
